# XCU exec
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The special built-in utilities are described inside
# utilities/V3_chap02.html (the page utilities/exec.html only redirects
# there), so anchors name V3_chap02.html and the .cov file accounts for
# the units by hand.

assertion  XCU.exec.001
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/redirections associated with the
class      required
says       With no utility operand, exec makes its redirections in the
           current shell: later commands write to the redirected output,
           read the redirected input, and use a newly opened descriptor.
test       t/001-redirect-only.sh

assertion  XCU.exec.002
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/shall execute a
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/shall not return to the shell
class      required
says       With a utility operand, exec replaces the shell with that
           utility: later commands are not run and the shell's exit status
           is the utility's.
test       t/002-replace-shell.sh

assertion  XCU.exec.003
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/<i>argument</i> operands (if any) as the command arguments
class      required
says       The operands after the utility name are its arguments, passed one
           to one (including empty ones and ones with spaces).
test       t/003-arguments.sh

assertion  XCU.exec.004
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES/Determine the search path
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.1.6
class      required
says       The utility operand is looked up through PATH; a script without a
           magic line found that way is run by a shell.
test       t/004-path.sh

assertion  XCU.exec.005
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/special built-in shall support XBD
class      required
since      2024
says       exec accepts "--" as the end of options before the utility.
test       t/005-double-hyphen.sh

assertion  XCU.exec.006
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/shall return a zero
class      required
says       exec with no operands, or with only redirections that succeed,
           returns status zero.
test       t/006-status-zero.sh

assertion  XCU.exec.007
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/If the
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/Non-built-in Utility Execution
class      required
says       exec of a utility that does not exist makes a non-interactive
           shell exit with status 127; no later command is run.
test       t/007-not-found.sh

assertion  XCU.exec.008
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/Non-built-in Utility Execution
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.2
class      required
says       exec of an existing file that is not executable makes a non-
           interactive shell exit with status 126.
test       t/008-not-executable.sh

assertion  XCU.exec.009
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#EXIT STATUS/redirection error occurs
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.8.1
class      required
says       A redirection error in exec makes a non-interactive shell exit
           with a status in the range 1 to 125.
test       t/009-redirect-error.sh

assertion  XCU.exec.010
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.9.1.6
class      required
says       exec in a subshell replaces only the subshell: the parent shell
           continues and sees the utility's status.
test       t/010-in-subshell.sh

assertion  XCU.exec.011
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#DESCRIPTION/an interactive shell may exit from a subshell
class      conditional
when       UP
says       A failing exec does not make an interactive shell exit (except
           from a subshell, where it may).
test       t/011-interactive-keeps-running.sh
